ter eq in the area with the king/fightersAnd I have both linked to my workstudy/areas room at the following:/wizards/gynter/areas.cthe links to the areas are marked as city1,city2enjoy :)/gynt' the friendly? wiz**Highvoltage**Subj: claanit sukkaaCc: kdfhDate: Feb  3eipa oo paljoo jarkee naissaakaan claaneís kuka hyvasa voi teha kakkos charrun ja teha sille claanin ja pkillia sita sittte ja saaha siita clan pojoi **Gynter** Re:   element areaDate: Feb  8nod I have seen the first ones.. was checking into it a little but thenI ended up with the trap-deamon and forgot about it totallyIt seems like when they executes the quests in the first room andcloses all exits the last exit(unclosable) changes its out toone of my worlds...  (will check into it and fix it tonight.. if I can)Now the last one with the spirit I think I have fixed,I noticed that I had forgotten the number 1 in set_mage(1)fixed that... will check it../gynt'**Gynter**Subj: exits changingDate: Feb  8I have a prob.When a player say's a special word he closes a portal to a partworld..but he doesn't really close it.. he just closes the name of the exitif I like have the exits sw,pillar,flames,hole,åppö(last should be pool)and then the player removes the exit flames. the only thing that happenedis that the exit flames is removed but then hole points to whereflames pointed too and pool points to where hole pointed tooand the plane that pool points too dissapearsIs there a way to check what exits that exist in a room?like this_object->exist_exit(\"flames\") would check if exit flames exist../gynt'**Sandtiger** Re:   money bug/wizingDate: Feb 15yes.. .. i know of a circumstance in the mud.. that yields money.... though i dont manipulate it.. nor use it.it has been present since the first day i have logged in.as for wizzing.. i'd like to.. but ... i have not much time with schooling and what not...so.. i would like to code.. but the time i can