rable to heal(spell)s.At first I thought that the target was invulnerable to all kinds of healsso that it also would not regenerate when that spell was in effect. Sadlyenough I've tested it and the target regenerates just as fast .. the onlydifference it makes is that a heal spell doesn't have any effect. Well,I know of only one or two mobs that heal themselves so this spell seemsto be a bit of a waiste like that. On the other hand, normal mobsregenerate hps quite fast so it seems a good idea to me that when the'chl alr les' spell is casted on a mob the speed of regeneration isreduced a lot.Please tell me if you don't like the idea, cheers Drude**Drude**Subj: 0 blowCc: lDate: Aug 30Anyhow this is what I got :)You are prepared to do the skill.The taste of blood fills your mouth as you focus your fury to the blow.You concentrate for a long time searching for the right timing and suddenlyscore a 0 blow to Guard's chest!Cheers**Atreyu**Subj: spellbookCc: celtron,irmeli,siki,nalle,wallaDate: Sep  1Hello,I think I have an idea that can be very useful and it is about thespellbook.At the moment when you merge a spell it is added to the end of thespellbook which is really nice. But it can be even nicer when thespells in the spellbook are sorted in some way. And I can think oftwo ways that can be useful:For instance, you can sort the spells in alphabetical order on thename of the spell .. likeabcrabacracarbaetc..Or you can sort them, in alphabetical order on the last spellword likeexs brr bltexs fla bltexs sol bltexs zzt bltexs brr zumetc..That last way has the advantage that you can see very fast which spellsare still missing in the spellbookThe other has the advantage that if some sells a scroll that you cansee very fast if you already have that scroll in your spellbook.having a sorted order in any case will help.THank you, atreyu**Drude**Subj: possible buggy parry?Cc: celtron,drude,irmeli,siki,nalle,wallaDate: Sep  5HiAs you know I log and count a lot so I found out that weapon parrydoesn't seem to work often, ie. it actually works rarely.This can be seen from the following stats that I have:(today I killed almost 75 giants ...)Total hits: 2034 (or 2030) ... this shows the number of rounds that I'vebeen in fight (times two)So I've been about 1000 rounds in a fight and did dodge,parry like:Dodge: 622,   Parry: 6 (weapon),  394 (shield)  and 15 partiallywhich shows that I'm able to dodge at least once every round or shieldparry but the weapon parry (which isn't at outstanding yet like theothers) doesn't do anything even when I choose to use the broad sword(which is a very light weapon).I'm not sure this is a bug since I'm fighting those giants and theyare supposed to be very strong which makes parrying more difficultbut I'd expect more succesful parries.If you have any questions on this then I might be able to answer them.Cheers, Drude**Drude**Subj: bug in postingCc: celtronDate: Sep  5Hi,It seems that most of my mails are going into thin air since theCC:thing of the mudmail doesn't work.When I enter: celtron,drude at it it just doesn't work.It tells me:Sending mail to Onarion.Sending mail to Celtron,drude.but I don't receive that mail which means that quite a number of my mailshaven't gone to the proper persons because the CC: stuff didn't work.Doing a CC: to only one person won't work either since one cannotforward mudmails ...Any question can be directed to me.Cheers, Drude**Rag**Subj: crash recoveryDate: Sep  6I heard that there was a crash recovery, but i didn't et anything back. Drude told me that you could reimburse me. Thank you, this mud rocks!**Rag**Subj: eqDate: Sep  8Thanks, here is the list; a bluish ring, ranger boots of forestry, thick bronwn belt, tyraels robes,iron bracers, iron chain gauntlets, 2x a dirty bronze flail, iron leggings, iron plate mail <white glow>.**Jenny**Sub